  "summary_en": "US Export Administration Regulations Part 742 sets license requirements and licensing policies for items on the Commerce Control List by reason for control (chemical/biological, nuclear, national security, missile technology, regional stability, crime control, anti-terrorism, encryption). It includes AI model weight controls (ECCN 4E091), advanced computing chip allocations, and robots in the Supplement 2 list.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "License required for AI model weights (ECCN 4E091) worldwide, with presumption of denial for end users outside listed countries",
   "Advanced computing items face country TPP allocations (790,000,000 TPP for 2025-2027) and presumption of denial for D:5/Macau",
   "Missile technology controls cover UAVs capable of 500 kg payload to 300 km",
   "Anti-terrorism controls on North Korea and Syria include robots capable of real-time feedback program modification",
   "Licensing reviewed under all applicable policies; approval only if all permit"
